  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NDC Partnership - core support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the NDC Partnership. Strenghtening the capacity of signatories to the Paris Agreement to enhance their NDCs and to implement activities necessary to fulfil the ambitions of their NDC.

The NDC Partnership assists developing countries in achieving and strengthening their nationally determined contribution (NDC) goals. The partnership identifies the countries&apos; needs and assists them in finding funding to meet them. Norway&apos;s support goes to implementing the partnership&apos;s work program for 2021-25. NDC-P is a collaboration between the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (UNFCCC), the World Resources Institute (WRI) and the United Nations Office for Project Management (UNOPS). NDC-P currently has over 190 members, both countries and development actors.</narrative>
  </description>
